<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Pure cross-cutting abstractions: marker interfaces (IAuditable), the event
    bus contract, and the neutral home for cross-module service interfaces.

    This project exists because of the three-project-per-module split. If Domain
    referenced NodeScope.Platform directly it would transitively depend on EF
    Core, and "the domain model does not know about persistence" would stop
    being true the moment the first module compiled. Splitting the interfaces
    out keeps that boundary a compile error rather than a convention.

    IRealtimeService lives here. Decision 2: this is the neutral home that lets
    permissions.service.ts:37 drop its moduleRef service-locator hack.

    Deliberately references nothing - not even Contracts.
  -->

</Project>
